1
00:01:05,300 --> 00:01:08,940
=When the Lights Rise=
=Episode 10=

2
00:01:25,220 --> 00:01:26,020
Mengde.

3
00:01:26,900 --> 00:01:30,420
Did you really only send women to him?

4
00:01:30,780 --> 00:01:32,020
You don't seriously think

5
00:01:32,980 --> 00:01:34,900
I arranged for a woman
to kill him, do you, Dad?

6
00:02:02,660 --> 00:02:06,340
Business certainly isn't easy
these days.

7
00:02:07,220 --> 00:02:10,780
Selling the department store
to the Japanese is one thing,

8
00:02:11,620 --> 00:02:13,620
but the tobacco business and the docks

9
00:02:14,460 --> 00:02:17,380
must remain in our hands.

10
00:02:18,220 --> 00:02:19,020
Of course.

11
00:02:21,020 --> 00:02:22,220
As long as you make sure

12
00:02:23,420 --> 00:02:25,460
my eldest sister stops bothering me,

13
00:02:26,660 --> 00:02:30,540
I'll make the Kuang family
greater than ever.

14
00:02:49,420 --> 00:02:51,340
Why are you siding
with them instead of me?

15
00:02:55,420 --> 00:02:56,380
Didn't you tell me

16
00:02:56,380 --> 00:02:57,820
to always listen to Grandfather?

17
00:02:58,380 --> 00:03:00,100
Since Grandfather likes Uncle Mengde,

18
00:03:01,380 --> 00:03:02,940
I should naturally respect him too.

19
00:03:03,060 --> 00:03:05,140
That monster is responsible
for your father's death.

20
00:03:07,420 --> 00:03:08,580
Not necessarily.

21
00:03:09,220 --> 00:03:11,980
Maybe Father was practically
asking to die.

22
00:03:12,820 --> 00:03:14,540
Kuang Yijie, how can you say that?

23
00:03:15,220 --> 00:03:16,220
Who taught you to talk like that?

24
00:03:18,460 --> 00:03:19,260
Mother.

25
00:03:20,620 --> 00:03:21,620
Just bear with it a little longer.

26
00:03:23,100 --> 00:03:26,700
Soon, it'll all be over.

27
00:03:56,880 --> 00:03:57,500
Who's there?

28
00:04:02,860 --> 00:04:03,780
Miss Mei, you...

29
00:04:11,480 --> 00:04:13,480
(St. Luke's Hospital)

30
00:04:25,620 --> 00:04:26,420
You're awake.

31
00:04:29,300 --> 00:04:30,220
Mr. Jing?

32
00:04:34,900 --> 00:04:36,060
What happened to me?

33
00:04:37,180 --> 00:04:38,340
You were exhausted last night.

34
00:04:38,380 --> 00:04:39,660
You stayed with Xiaozhu all night

35
00:04:39,820 --> 00:04:41,540
and passed out from exhaustion.

36
00:04:45,690 --> 00:04:46,940
Your clothes were dirty yesterday,

37
00:04:47,150 --> 00:04:48,530
so I had someone get you changed.

38
00:04:49,740 --> 00:04:50,340
Thank you.

39
00:04:54,580 --> 00:04:55,700
What brings you here too?

40
00:04:57,420 --> 00:04:58,500
I was worried about you,

41
00:04:59,220 --> 00:05:00,180
so I came to check on you.

42
00:05:01,620 --> 00:05:03,340
The doctor prescribed
this to help you relax.

43
00:05:04,020 --> 00:05:04,900
I'll leave it here.

44
00:05:13,820 --> 00:05:15,660
I feel perfectly fine.

45
00:05:16,020 --> 00:05:17,540
I should be able to go home now, right?

46
00:05:17,580 --> 00:05:18,380
- Yes.
- Yes.

47
00:05:23,060 --> 00:05:24,180
My car is downstairs.

48
00:05:24,420 --> 00:05:25,700
I'll take you back to the tailor shop.

49
00:05:26,260 --> 00:05:27,500
The tailor shop isn't safe.

50
00:05:27,620 --> 00:05:29,500
Miss Mei should stay
at my place for now.

51
00:05:30,060 --> 00:05:31,180
That way, someone can look after her.

52
00:05:33,060 --> 00:05:34,580
Stay at your place?

53
00:05:34,580 --> 00:05:35,380
Yes.

54
00:05:39,960 --> 00:05:42,780
I've certainly made quite
a few enemies lately.

55
00:05:43,180 --> 00:05:44,220
I should be more careful.

56
00:05:44,300 --> 00:05:45,620
The tailor shop is perfectly safe now.

57
00:05:45,620 --> 00:05:46,860
I can take you back whenever you like.

58
00:05:55,660 --> 00:05:56,980
If you need any help,

59
00:05:57,580 --> 00:05:59,060
you can always find me
at the Cishan Foundation.

60
00:06:00,300 --> 00:06:01,660
Sorry to trouble you, Mr. Jing.

61
00:06:16,900 --> 00:06:19,220
Jing Fanshu was at the hospital
all night?

62
00:06:19,640 --> 00:06:20,040
Yes.

63
00:06:20,860 --> 00:06:22,220
He was already there when I arrived.

64
00:06:25,420 --> 00:06:26,860
Did you two know each other before?

65
00:06:27,660 --> 00:06:28,740
Not really.

66
00:06:29,500 --> 00:06:32,540
He funded Xiaozhu's scholarship.

67
00:06:33,220 --> 00:06:35,540
But I'd never dealt
with him directly before.

68
00:06:37,260 --> 00:06:38,020
And I don't know

69
00:06:38,020 --> 00:06:39,340
why someone like him

70
00:06:39,820 --> 00:06:41,580
would care about Xiaozhu's death.

71
00:06:42,500 --> 00:06:43,820
Perhaps what concerns him

72
00:06:44,300 --> 00:06:45,980
isn't just Xiaozhu's death.

73
00:06:46,220 --> 00:06:47,020
What do you mean?

74
00:06:47,460 --> 00:06:49,100
You'd better not get too close to him.

75
00:06:49,220 --> 00:06:51,100
He may not be involved
in the Kun Society's business,

76
00:06:51,180 --> 00:06:52,820
but he's still one of them.

77
00:06:53,220 --> 00:06:55,100
And Boss Ren is his adoptive father.

78
00:06:56,220 --> 00:06:58,220
Don't actually think of him
as a philanthropist.

79
00:06:59,780 --> 00:07:00,580
I know.

80
00:07:01,420 --> 00:07:01,930
By the way,

81
00:07:02,820 --> 00:07:04,620
what did Boss Ren
want with you last night?

82
00:07:04,620 --> 00:07:05,900
He asked me to investigate Lv Mengde.

83
00:07:06,060 --> 00:07:06,860
Really?

84
00:07:08,620 --> 00:07:10,020
Looks like our plan is working.

85
00:07:11,980 --> 00:07:12,780
That's great.

86
00:07:13,460 --> 00:07:15,020
As long as we make Boss Ren

87
00:07:15,060 --> 00:07:16,740
start to suspect Lv Mengde,

88
00:07:17,660 --> 00:07:19,460
we can use that suspicion

89
00:07:19,580 --> 00:07:20,820
to turn them against each other.

90
00:07:22,020 --> 00:07:23,620
What are you planning to do next?

91
00:07:23,980 --> 00:07:26,420
Should we tell Boss Ren

92
00:07:26,580 --> 00:07:27,580
about the black powder?

93
00:07:28,580 --> 00:07:29,900
The time isn't right yet.

94
00:07:30,700 --> 00:07:33,420
I heard Lv Mengde is helping Boss Ren

95
00:07:33,420 --> 00:07:35,700
broker a deal between the Kuang family
and the Japanese Chamber of Commerce.

96
00:07:36,220 --> 00:07:37,940
Since Boss Ren asked me to investigate,

97
00:07:37,980 --> 00:07:39,620
he clearly doesn't want
to alert Lv Mengde.

98
00:07:41,100 --> 00:07:41,900
Come in.

99
00:07:42,750 --> 00:07:43,500
All right.

100
00:07:43,500 --> 00:07:44,420
Something smells delicious.

101
00:07:44,420 --> 00:07:45,140
Yiyi?

102
00:07:49,380 --> 00:07:50,540
Wash your hands. It's time to eat.

103
00:07:51,780 --> 00:07:53,980
You two sure know when to come home.

104
00:07:54,420 --> 00:07:56,300
Yiyi made all these dishes.

105
00:07:56,620 --> 00:07:58,340
The fish just came off the stove.

106
00:07:59,860 --> 00:08:00,980
Yiyi's back.

107
00:08:01,580 --> 00:08:02,580
This morning,

108
00:08:02,700 --> 00:08:03,660
when I went downstairs,

109
00:08:03,820 --> 00:08:05,500
she was already in the courtyard.

110
00:08:08,980 --> 00:08:09,780
Were you hurt?

111
00:08:09,780 --> 00:08:10,820
I'm fine.

112
00:08:11,620 --> 00:08:12,700
When did you get back?

113
00:08:13,020 --> 00:08:13,980
Go wait outside for now.

114
00:08:13,980 --> 00:08:14,940
The food's almost ready.

115
00:08:26,300 --> 00:08:27,180
Stop staring.

116
00:08:28,100 --> 00:08:28,980
Let's eat.

117
00:08:29,300 --> 00:08:30,420
The food's getting cold.

118
00:08:34,500 --> 00:08:36,060
Right, let's eat.

119
00:08:37,300 --> 00:08:38,860
Yiyi's cooking is really good.

120
00:08:39,420 --> 00:08:40,300
Have some more.

121
00:08:45,340 --> 00:08:46,140
Here, Yiyi.

122
00:08:46,500 --> 00:08:47,460
You should eat more too.

123
00:08:47,820 --> 00:08:49,780
After we eat, I'll take you
to the hospital.

124
00:08:51,020 --> 00:08:52,050
I've already been to the hospital.

125
00:08:54,330 --> 00:08:55,500
The doctor said it was nothing serious

126
00:08:55,500 --> 00:08:56,460
and I didn't need treatment.

127
00:08:57,180 --> 00:08:58,420
Which hospital did you go to?

128
00:08:58,820 --> 00:08:59,980
Which doctor did you see?

129
00:08:59,980 --> 00:09:01,780
The French doctor
at St. Luke's Hospital.

130
00:09:03,100 --> 00:09:04,020
Her name was Bai something.

131
00:09:04,020 --> 00:09:04,820
Bai Mali.

132
00:09:05,060 --> 00:09:05,900
You know her?

133
00:09:07,220 --> 00:09:08,340
Mr. Jing knows her.

134
00:09:10,300 --> 00:09:12,540
She was the one who tended
to Xiaozhu yesterday.

135
00:09:13,620 --> 00:09:14,740
Jing Fanshu.

136
00:09:16,620 --> 00:09:18,060
Where have you been these past few days?

137
00:09:18,260 --> 00:09:19,220
What did the doctor say?

138
00:09:24,380 --> 00:09:25,220
Enough.

139
00:09:25,220 --> 00:09:26,380
What matters is that she's back.

140
00:09:26,420 --> 00:09:27,100
Stop asking questions.

141
00:09:27,620 --> 00:09:29,660
Can't you let Yiyi eat in peace?

142
00:09:29,900 --> 00:09:30,700
Tell me.

143
00:09:30,980 --> 00:09:31,780
You said

144
00:09:33,220 --> 00:09:34,620
that if I saw a doctor,

145
00:09:35,500 --> 00:09:36,700
you'd leave me alone.

146
00:09:37,020 --> 00:09:38,180
I've seen one now.

147
00:09:40,550 --> 00:09:41,220
Yiyi.

148
00:09:42,820 --> 00:09:44,660
Why are you so stubborn?

149
00:09:44,860 --> 00:09:46,740
Yiyi's only just started feeling better.

150
00:09:47,060 --> 00:09:48,860
And you're bringing all this up again.

151
00:09:48,980 --> 00:09:50,380
She's hiding something from me.

152
00:09:50,420 --> 00:09:51,900
Everyone has things
they keep to themselves.

153
00:09:52,180 --> 00:09:54,060
We just need to spend more time

154
00:09:54,060 --> 00:09:55,460
talking things through with her.

155
00:09:55,820 --> 00:09:57,900
What can't be resolved by talking?

156
00:10:02,020 --> 00:10:02,820
Miss Mei.

157
00:10:03,380 --> 00:10:05,140
Your sister's funeral is tomorrow.

158
00:10:05,420 --> 00:10:06,940
Shouldn't you go back and prepare?

159
00:10:07,460 --> 00:10:08,780
There's nothing much to prepare.

160
00:10:09,260 --> 00:10:11,940
Besides, the funeral isn't
what matters most.

161
00:10:12,020 --> 00:10:13,020
You're still going to investigate?

162
00:10:15,620 --> 00:10:17,340
Then let me make one thing clear.

163
00:10:17,700 --> 00:10:18,780
What happened to your sister

164
00:10:18,780 --> 00:10:20,340
has nothing to do with the Ding family.

165
00:10:20,420 --> 00:10:22,380
You're free to investigate on your own.

166
00:10:22,380 --> 00:10:23,940
But could I please ask you

167
00:10:23,980 --> 00:10:25,860
to stop dragging Ding Zhao into it?

168
00:10:25,860 --> 00:10:26,620
Uncle.

169
00:10:26,900 --> 00:10:28,100
It's true, though.

170
00:10:28,100 --> 00:10:29,580
You're investigating day after day,

171
00:10:29,580 --> 00:10:30,820
and you've even offended Boss Lv.

172
00:10:30,820 --> 00:10:32,220
Only by finding out the truth

173
00:10:32,220 --> 00:10:33,420
can we put an end to this.

174
00:10:33,420 --> 00:10:35,020
Are you a police officer or a detective?

175
00:10:35,020 --> 00:10:36,500
You keep going out of your way
to cause trouble,

176
00:10:36,660 --> 00:10:39,420
and with powerful people
in Shanghai, no less.

177
00:10:39,420 --> 00:10:41,020
If you don't get back on the right path,

178
00:10:41,420 --> 00:10:43,180
you'll have a hard time ahead.

179
00:10:45,660 --> 00:10:46,540
Just look at this.

180
00:10:46,860 --> 00:10:48,300
Now even lowlifes

181
00:10:48,300 --> 00:10:49,620
dare to refuse to repay their debts.

182
00:10:49,620 --> 00:10:51,300
They're all hoping we'll suffer
some terrible misfortune

183
00:10:51,380 --> 00:10:52,620
so their debts will be wiped out.

184
00:10:54,580 --> 00:10:55,860
Why don't you go check on things?

185
00:10:56,860 --> 00:10:58,700
Don't take what my uncle said to heart.

186
00:10:58,980 --> 00:11:01,420
Actually, he's not wrong.

187
00:11:02,260 --> 00:11:03,500
You and I are different.

188
00:11:04,380 --> 00:11:05,900
I have no family left.

189
00:11:06,180 --> 00:11:08,180
Investigating this case is all
that keeps me going.

190
00:11:08,780 --> 00:11:10,380
But you still have family
you care about.

191
00:11:10,380 --> 00:11:12,220
You can still live a good life.

192
00:11:14,820 --> 00:11:17,060
Do you know why
I'm investigating this case?

193
00:11:18,420 --> 00:11:19,660
If it's to collect a debt,

194
00:11:20,420 --> 00:11:21,860
you and I have already
settled our accounts.

195
00:11:22,820 --> 00:11:23,700
If it's for your sister,

196
00:11:23,700 --> 00:11:24,860
she's back now.

197
00:11:24,860 --> 00:11:25,900
As for Lv Mengde,

198
00:11:27,100 --> 00:11:28,420
your sister likes him,

199
00:11:30,020 --> 00:11:31,260
but I want him dead.

200
00:11:32,300 --> 00:11:34,260
I've already promised
Boss Ren I'd investigate him.

201
00:11:34,820 --> 00:11:36,500
We're after the same thing.

202
00:11:36,500 --> 00:11:37,300
No, we're not.

203
00:11:38,180 --> 00:11:39,380
My investigation is different
from yours.

204
00:11:39,820 --> 00:11:40,740
That list

205
00:11:41,060 --> 00:11:43,340
involves more than just
Lv Mengde and Dong Zhenglun.

206
00:11:44,300 --> 00:11:45,900
Even if you're not doing it
for your sister,

207
00:11:45,900 --> 00:11:47,700
your business depends
on the Kun Society.

208
00:11:47,780 --> 00:11:50,380
You can't possibly take on
the entire Kun Society.

209
00:11:56,420 --> 00:11:57,740
We're not on the same side.

210
00:11:59,020 --> 00:12:00,340
It's best we part ways
sooner rather than later.

211
00:12:04,380 --> 00:12:05,180
Mr. Ding.

212
00:12:05,780 --> 00:12:06,820
Thank you

213
00:12:07,020 --> 00:12:07,900
for everything you've done.

214
00:12:28,420 --> 00:12:29,220
Mengde.

215
00:12:30,220 --> 00:12:31,460
Let's consider today's meal

216
00:12:31,860 --> 00:12:35,700
a celebration
of your name being cleared.

217
00:12:38,500 --> 00:12:40,580
I have you to thank, Dad,

218
00:12:40,580 --> 00:12:42,220
and Boss Ren for seeing things clearly.

219
00:12:46,020 --> 00:12:46,820
By the way,

220
00:12:47,420 --> 00:12:48,340
that woman,

221
00:12:48,700 --> 00:12:50,460
how do you plan to deal with her?

222
00:12:50,870 --> 00:12:51,380
There's no rush.

223
00:12:52,220 --> 00:12:54,660
The funeral is for the public to see.

224
00:12:54,900 --> 00:12:55,700
As for her life,

225
00:12:57,420 --> 00:12:58,860
we'll leave that until then.

226
00:13:00,700 --> 00:13:01,500
Very well.

227
00:13:02,620 --> 00:13:03,940
That way, her blood won't

228
00:13:04,220 --> 00:13:05,780
spoil our joyous occasion.

229
00:13:07,020 --> 00:13:08,460
I've consulted someone
about an auspicious date.

230
00:13:09,020 --> 00:13:11,220
There's a good day coming up.

231
00:13:11,460 --> 00:13:13,860
I'll have the Sanshi Club

232
00:13:14,580 --> 00:13:17,460
arrange a ceremony
to welcome you into the family.

233
00:13:17,700 --> 00:13:20,020
After that, you'll take
the Kuang surname

234
00:13:20,420 --> 00:13:22,500
and be known as Kuang Mengde.

235
00:13:29,100 --> 00:13:29,900
Thank you, Dad.

236
00:13:32,300 --> 00:13:33,300
Congratulations, Uncle Mengde.

237
00:13:34,820 --> 00:13:35,660
Congratulations, Grandfather.

238
00:13:36,300 --> 00:13:37,100
Yijie.

239
00:13:37,620 --> 00:13:38,940
After everything that's happened,

240
00:13:39,620 --> 00:13:40,900
you've really grown up.

241
00:13:42,220 --> 00:13:44,300
Try to persuade your mother

242
00:13:44,590 --> 00:13:45,920
to change that awful temper of hers.

243
00:13:47,380 --> 00:13:48,500
We're all family.

244
00:13:48,780 --> 00:13:50,380
Harmony brings prosperity, after all.

245
00:13:50,580 --> 00:13:51,340
I understand, Grandfather.

246
00:13:51,980 --> 00:13:52,780
Good boy.

247
00:13:53,380 --> 00:13:54,660
Stick with your uncle from now on.

248
00:13:55,260 --> 00:13:57,860
I'll make sure
you're well taken care of.

249
00:13:57,860 --> 00:13:58,740
Thank you, Uncle Mengde.

250
00:14:08,970 --> 00:14:09,980
Sir, everything's taken care of.

251
00:14:11,420 --> 00:14:12,380
What about the men lying in wait?

252
00:14:12,780 --> 00:14:13,580
We've identified them too.

253
00:14:13,580 --> 00:14:15,700
They were hired by Director Kong
and Bank President Qin.

254
00:14:17,420 --> 00:14:18,300
Take care of them.

255
00:14:18,500 --> 00:14:19,940
How could you be so foolish?

256
00:14:20,100 --> 00:14:21,940
Who told you to kill Mei Yuhe?

257
00:14:22,020 --> 00:14:24,020
We were afraid she'd uncover
what we'd done.

258
00:14:25,100 --> 00:14:26,420
If you're going to kill someone,
do it properly.

259
00:14:26,460 --> 00:14:27,860
A failed attempt only leaves us exposed.

260
00:14:31,060 --> 00:14:32,980
What about Boss Lv?

261
00:14:33,780 --> 00:14:34,620
What did he say?

262
00:14:34,620 --> 00:14:35,340
Exactly.

263
00:14:35,420 --> 00:14:37,580
Is he just going to ignore this?

264
00:14:37,660 --> 00:14:39,060
He'll handle it himself.

265
00:14:40,100 --> 00:14:41,900
Don't cause him any more trouble.

266
00:14:44,660 --> 00:14:45,780
Not just the shop.

267
00:14:46,120 --> 00:14:47,780
This entire building

268
00:14:48,060 --> 00:14:49,260
belongs to you now.

269
00:14:50,100 --> 00:14:50,580
What?

270
00:14:50,860 --> 00:14:52,460
A gentleman bought it for you.

271
00:14:52,620 --> 00:14:53,460
From now on,

272
00:14:53,620 --> 00:14:55,660
you're our landlord.

273
00:14:55,930 --> 00:14:57,900
Which gentleman? What's his surname?

274
00:14:58,060 --> 00:14:59,520
Oh, he didn't say.

275
00:14:59,700 --> 00:15:01,460
He didn't look like a grown man, though.

276
00:15:01,820 --> 00:15:03,860
He was only seventeen
or eighteen at most.

277
00:15:03,860 --> 00:15:06,220
He must be some family's young master.

278
00:15:07,340 --> 00:15:08,500
Young Master...

279
00:15:10,060 --> 00:15:10,860
Miss Mei.

280
00:15:12,940 --> 00:15:14,660
I'll let you get back to work.

281
00:15:19,140 --> 00:15:22,220
Looks like that young gentleman
gave you this too.

282
00:15:22,420 --> 00:15:24,460
I'll leave you to it. Goodbye.

283
00:15:24,660 --> 00:15:25,460
Goodbye.

284
00:15:42,320 --> 00:15:43,440
(Teahouse Girl's Suicide Note Points
to Real Killer in the Concessions)

285
00:15:43,440 --> 00:15:44,360
(Rumors of Cat Woman Possession:
Fact or Fiction?)

286
00:15:44,360 --> 00:15:45,160
(Shanghai Rumors Hint
at Secrets of the Powerful)

287
00:15:45,160 --> 00:15:46,080
(Schoolgirl Takes Her Own Life
at Home After Mental Breakdown)

288
00:15:46,080 --> 00:15:48,000
(Terror at the Dance Hall: Another
Beauty Lost Beneath the Neon Lights)

289
00:15:53,440 --> 00:15:55,640
(See You at the Funeral)

290
00:16:04,060 --> 00:16:04,980
Wait!

291
00:16:06,020 --> 00:16:06,820
Wait a minute!

292
00:16:09,940 --> 00:16:10,740
Wait a minute!

293
00:16:11,740 --> 00:16:12,740
You gave me the evidence.

294
00:16:12,740 --> 00:16:14,100
Why won't you work with me?

295
00:16:14,380 --> 00:16:15,100
I know.

296
00:16:15,100 --> 00:16:16,420
You don't want to reveal your identity.

297
00:16:16,420 --> 00:16:18,420
But isn't it even more dangerous
to act alone?

298
00:16:19,100 --> 00:16:19,900
Stop!

299
00:16:31,140 --> 00:16:31,940
Stop!

300
00:17:17,960 --> 00:17:22,130
♪Neon lights shimmer across my body♪

301
00:17:24,160 --> 00:17:25,870
♪Like diamonds flickering♪

302
00:17:26,500 --> 00:17:27,420
Mr. Jing?

303
00:17:32,160 --> 00:17:36,270
♪My high heels tap against the streets
of the old harbor♪

304
00:17:38,200 --> 00:17:43,100
♪Every step is marked by blood,
sweat, and hardship♪

305
00:17:46,360 --> 00:17:49,790
♪They pour a word or two of lies
into their wineglasses♪

306
00:17:49,880 --> 00:17:50,510
♪And say to me♪

307
00:17:50,520 --> 00:17:53,470
♪Come on, smile. Don't ask why♪

308
00:17:53,480 --> 00:17:55,910
♪But I can clearly taste the rust♪

309
00:17:55,920 --> 00:18:01,870
♪Behind the cold, cloying champagne♪

310
00:18:02,470 --> 00:18:05,190
♪I once witnessed demons♪

311
00:18:05,200 --> 00:18:08,550
♪Selling hope amid applause♪

312
00:18:08,940 --> 00:18:11,240
♪If this is what they call salvation♪

313
00:18:11,500 --> 00:18:12,670
♪Then I would rather choose♪

314
00:18:12,670 --> 00:18:14,950
♪To wake amid pain and blood♪

315
00:18:15,680 --> 00:18:18,720
♪And watch the lights
come on one by one♪

316
00:18:19,280 --> 00:18:22,120
♪Like blades cutting
through the radiance♪

317
00:18:22,760 --> 00:18:25,600
♪You may treat me as dust
beneath your feet♪

318
00:18:25,600 --> 00:18:27,520
♪Or wipe me away like ashes♪

319
00:18:27,520 --> 00:18:29,080
♪Leaving a cold ending♪

320
00:18:29,080 --> 00:18:31,040
♪But I refuse to fall♪

321
00:18:31,040 --> 00:18:35,960
♪I refuse to become a shadow
fading beneath the lights♪

322
00:18:36,080 --> 00:18:38,520
♪I refuse to dissolve into♪

323
00:18:39,600 --> 00:18:42,600
♪The lifeless light of the past♪

324
00:18:42,920 --> 00:18:45,760
♪I want sharpness at my fingertips♪

325
00:18:45,800 --> 00:18:48,600
♪And steps that avoid
the traps among the thorns♪

326
00:18:49,320 --> 00:18:52,200
♪At dawn, I will look
straight into your eyes♪

327
00:18:52,200 --> 00:18:55,400
♪My gaze clear, illuminating the dawn♪

328
00:18:56,880 --> 00:18:59,640
♪Those who have hurt me♪

329
00:19:00,200 --> 00:19:02,880
♪I choose to pierce through♪

330
00:19:04,480 --> 00:19:05,960
♪To tear apart♪

331
00:19:06,080 --> 00:19:11,960
♪To ignite a sacred flame♪

332
00:19:13,640 --> 00:19:15,760
♪I do not pray to the gods♪

333
00:19:15,760 --> 00:19:18,680
♪Nor bow to power♪

334
00:19:18,680 --> 00:19:20,960
♪I will no longer play the tragic lead♪

335
00:19:22,760 --> 00:19:26,680
♪I will stand and carve
the path of my own fate♪
